<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Adding column vectors</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\mathbf{a} = {@col(av)@}\), \(\mathbf{b} = {@col(bv)@}\) and \(\mathbf{c} = {@col(cv)@}\).</p><p>(a) Find \(\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b}\).</p><div>\(\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find \(\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{c}\).</p><div>\(\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{c} =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Add across with across and up with up.</p><p>(a) Top: \([[if test="is(b1<0)"]]{@a1@} + ({@b1@})[[else]]{@a1@} + {@b1@}[[/if]] = {@a1+b1@}\). Bottom: \([[if test="is(b2<0)"]]{@a2@} + ({@b2@})[[else]]{@a2@} + {@b2@}[[/if]] = {@a2+b2@}\). So \(\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} = {@s@}\).</p><p>(b) Add \(\mathbf{c}\) to your answer to (a): \({@s@} + {@col(cv)@} = {@s3@}\).</p><p>Drawn head to tail, the resultant goes from the tail of \(\mathbf{a}\) to the head of the last vector.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
col(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]]);
/* Design: add column vectors by components, with a third vector. Example 4.1's pair a = (5, -3), b = (-2, 6) is excluded (b2 # 6 when a = (5, -3) and b1 = -2). Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Section B. */
a1: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0]); a2: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0]);
b1: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0,a1]);
b2: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0, if a1=5 and a2=-3 and b1=-2 then 6 elseif a1=4 and a2=-1 and b1=-3 then 4 else 0]);

cc1: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0]); cc2: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0]);
av: [a1,a2]; bv: [b1,b2]; cv: [cc1,cc2];
s: col(av+bv); dif: col(av-bv); dif2: col(bv-av);
s3: col(av+bv+cv); sub3: col(av+bv-cv);
tw1: s+matrix([1],[0]); ft2: s3+matrix([1],[0]); tw3: s3+matrix([0],[1]);
badm: matrix([q],[1]);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
